CHAPTER.VERS:
Blow ye 

          He shows the great judgments of God which are at hand, unless they repent.
         the trumpet in Zion, and sound an alarm in my holy mountain: let all the inhabitants of the land tremble: for the day of the LORD cometh, for [it is] nigh at hand;

Who knoweth [if] he will 

          He speaks this to stir up their slothfulness, and not that he doubted of God's mercies, if they did repent. For the way in which God repents, {{See Jer_18:8}}
         return and repent, and leave a blessing behind him; [even] a meat offering and a drink offering unto the LORD your God?
